1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,795
Why is there a tiny hole in

2
00:00:01,795 --> 00:00:03,192
your airplane window?

3
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:04,743
It looks like a mistake,

4
00:00:04,743 --> 00:00:06,855
but it is keeping the window working.

5
00:00:07,035 --> 00:00:09,938
An airplane window is not one pane.

6
00:00:10,118 --> 00:00:11,000
It is three.

7
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:13,398
The inner one is just a scratch

8
00:00:13,398 --> 00:00:13,827
guard.

9
00:00:14,007 --> 00:00:16,007
The middle and outer panes are the

10
00:00:16,007 --> 00:00:16,712
real window.

11
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:17,930
The tiny hole,

12
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:20,672
called a breather hole or bleed hole,

13
00:00:20,672 --> 00:00:22,303
is in the middle pane.

14
00:00:22,483 --> 00:00:25,165
It lets the air pressure between the

15
00:00:25,165 --> 00:00:26,804
panes match the cabin,

16
00:00:26,804 --> 00:00:28,368
so during the flight,

17
00:00:28,368 --> 00:00:31,125
the cabin pressure pushes only on the

18
00:00:31,125 --> 00:00:31,945
outer pane.

19
00:00:32,125 --> 00:00:34,876
The middle pane carries almost nothing.

20
00:00:35,056 --> 00:00:36,260
It is a spare,

21
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:39,184
waiting in case the outer one ever

22
00:00:39,184 --> 00:00:39,700
fails.

23
00:00:40,051 --> 00:00:41,734
Think about what that means.

24
00:00:41,914 --> 00:00:44,350
At cruise, the air outside is thin

25
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:47,073
and cold, and the cabin is pressurized

26
00:00:47,073 --> 00:00:49,437
so that you can breathe normally.

27
00:00:49,617 --> 00:00:52,752
That difference in pressure pushes outward on

28
00:00:52,752 --> 00:00:54,633
every window, every flight,

29
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:57,071
thousands of times over the life of

30
00:00:57,071 --> 00:00:57,976
the airplane.

31
00:00:58,156 --> 00:01:00,731
By loading only one pane and keeping

32
00:01:00,731 --> 00:01:02,447
a second one in reserve,

33
00:01:02,447 --> 00:01:05,022
the designers built a backup that is

34
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:07,096
always there and never tired.

35
00:01:07,276 --> 00:01:09,073
If the outer pane cracks,

36
00:01:09,073 --> 00:01:11,015
the middle pane takes over.
